2. SecurityConfig

The SecurityConfig class configures Spring Security.

@Configuration
@EnableWebSecurity
public class SecurityConfig extends WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter
Main Functions
Creates in-memory users.
Encrypts passwords.
Configures security rules.
Adds JWT Authorization Filter.
In-Memory Users
Username : admin
Password : pwd
Role     : ADMIN

Username : user
Password : pwd
Role     : USER
Password Encoder
@Bean
public PasswordEncoder passwordEncoder() {
    return new BCryptPasswordEncoder();
}

Encrypts passwords using BCrypt.

HttpSecurity Configuration
Disable CSRF
Enable Basic Authentication
Protect /authenticate
Add JWT Filter
3. AuthenticationController

Handles user authentication and generates a JWT token.

Endpoint
GET /authenticate
Working
Receives Authorization Header.
Decodes username and password.
Extracts username.
Generates JWT token.
Returns token to the client.

Example Response

{
   "token":"eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..."
}
4. JwtAuthorizationFilter

This filter validates the JWT token before allowing access.

Functions
Reads Authorization Header.
Checks whether the token starts with Bearer.
Validates the JWT.
Extracts username.
Stores authentication in SecurityContextHolder.

If the token is invalid, access is denied.

5. Country Controller

Provides REST APIs for country information.

Endpoints
